	"_about": "The chapter openers (src/opener.gd): a short cinematic before each campaign chapter's first tick, the camera flown over the level, a title card, the boss in silhouette, an old storyteller reading two lines (ElevenLabs voice \"narrator\", an original character), and the camera brought down into the player's eyes as play starts. Looks only. Read by scripts/audio_spec.py (the lines) and the game. Cues: narr_<chapter>_<n> (the lines), opener_<chapter>_hit (the card's hit; hit_lead: seconds into it of the hit), sting_open_<chapter> (the music when the chapter's song is not there). Shots (src/opener_camera.gd): path is where the camera flies and look what it watches, each a list of [x, y, z] keys (cells; z the height, the ground about 0, roofs 2 to 3) it passes smoothly through, at an even speed easing in and out (ease: the speed at the start and end, a share of the cruise), the gaze a little ahead; secs how long; amb the ambience under it (amb_<amb>, else the chapter's amb, else the level's own); spots [seconds into the shot, cue, volume, pan] its own sounds. title: when the card drops (s); boss: the cel (art name), the light behind it, its growl, its sting and its line. mix (src/opener_mix.gd): the bed's hold at its moments (a share of MUSIC VOLUME: start, the card landing, between, the reveal, the dip under the boss's sting, the landing; play's level at the end), the whooshes at the cuts, the reveal's swell, the boss sting's, the hits' and far-off sounds' volumes.",
